&lt;p&gt;As Senior Manager, Data Privacy, you will act as a trusted advisor to the business, providing pragmatic and commercially-focused privacy guidance across departments. Working closely with stakeholders globally, you will play a key role in supporting the organisation to manage personal data responsibly, maintain compliance, and fortify consistent, high-quality data protection practices across the business.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;br&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll do:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Draft and negotiate one-off data-share agreements (e.g., artists, distribution clients, ticketing partners, co-promoters)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Review, draft and negotiate vendor agreement data protection provisions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct and document Privacy Impact Assessments and Transfer Impact Assessments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advise business stakeholders on the compliant use of approved third-party tools and services&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the Product Design &amp;amp; Engineering team on the development and global implementation of internal tools&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;M&amp;amp;A data privacy due diligence, contract review, and post-acquisition integration support&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Incident response support&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Review data import and export requests&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support Sony Music’s live division, including negotiating vendor, location, co-promotion and IP license agreements, drafting privacy notices and marketing consent language, and collaborating with other Sony Group companies on Sony IP location-based events&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advise label marketing teams on local and multi-market contests, including compliance with applicable data privacy and marketing legislation and codes of practice&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support label and international marketing teams on promotional campaigns, ensuring compliance with applicable data privacy and marketing legislation and music/streaming chart rules&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with the business to prepare Data Subject Access Requests responses&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the Customer Relationship Management team with data rights requests and scheduled data deletion&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advise the People Experience team on local and company-wide initiatives, including internal surveys, employee tools and services, and the global careers site&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support US and International litigation teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2 class=&quot;iCIMS_InfoMsg iCIMS_InfoField_Job&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Essential:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A minimum of two years’ PQE, preferably in the Data Privacy field&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Handling Data Subject Access Requests&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Preparing Privacy Impact Assessments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drafting and negotiating data processing agreements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Implementing and maintaining data privacy operations (e.g., ROPAs, PI inventories, automated processes)&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience advising digital marketing teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge and awareness of ongoing developments related to Data Privacy law worldwide, including but not limited to EU/UK, US, APAC, LatAm&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent analytical and communication skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work with others within Sony Group and across Sony Music divisions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong negotiation skills and work ethic&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Team player with strong interpersonal skills, emotional intelligence, good judgment, and intellectual curiosity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to build trusted advisor relationships with internal clients, together with commitment to provide the highest quality internal client support&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Desirable:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;IAPP certifications (including Cyber and AI)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in Incident Response&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working in the entertainment/media industry&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of AI and marketing legislation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Powerpoint skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
